# Derivatives

The operators that differentiate: partial derivatives of any order, derivatives with respect to a complex variable, the gradient, Jacobian and Hessian, and the covariant derivative of a scalar field. Every derivative is exact: the rules are applied to the recorded formula.

## The Surface

| Symbol | What it is |
|---|---|
| [`conjugate_wirtinger`](differential/conjugate_wirtinger.md) | The conjugate Wirtinger derivative `∂/∂z̄`; it vanishes exactly where a function is holomorphic. |
| [`covariant`](differential/covariant.md) | The covariant derivative of a scalar field along one variable: `∂f/∂x + Γ f`. |
| [`differential`](differential/differential.md) | The partial derivative of a function with respect to one variable, to any order. |
| [`gradient`](differential/gradient.md) | The vector of first partial derivatives of a scalar function. |
| [`hessian`](differential/hessian.md) | The matrix of second partial derivatives of a scalar function. |
| [`jacobian`](differential/jacobian.md) | The matrix of first partial derivatives of a vector-valued function. |
| [`magnitude_differential`](differential/magnitude_differential.md) | The absolute value of a derivative: `|f⁽ⁿ⁾|`. |
| [`wirtinger`](differential/wirtinger.md) | The Wirtinger derivative `∂/∂z` of a function of a complex variable. |

